chunk_s": 380250.9349883, "t_first_token_s": 380250.9349883, "t_start_s": 380250.8787207, "text": "A GPU (Graphics Processing Unit) outperforms a CPU (Central Processing Unit) at matrix multiplication due to its specialized architecture and parallel processing capabilities. Unlike CPUs, which execute instructions sequentially, GPUs are designed to handle massive parallel computations, making them ideal for matrix multiplication. Each GPU core can perform thousands of calculations simultaneously, leveraging the massive number of cores and threads available. This allows GPUs to execute matrix multiplication much faster than CPUs, as the parallel processing enables the simultaneous execution of multiple operations, reducing the overall computation time.", "total_duration_ns": 994021600, "ttft_s": 0.056267600040882826, "valid": true}
